        "id": 11132,
        "name": "ellindar",
        "username": "ellindar",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/a4c791/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-24T04:39:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p><span>So my son and I broke it out for the first time tonight (purchased at gencon)&nbsp;</span><br><br><span>He took citizen dawn without the scenario powers, I took ra. First to 3 incaps wins. (skirmish)</span><br><br><span>All I can say is it wasn't even close to a contest. Citizen Dawn won so easily that it was more than ridiculous. So, either the villains aren't meant to be played in skirmish mode, or we seriously are messing something up.&nbsp;</span><br><br><span>I mean Citizen dawn puts out a citizen with one action that has 8 health itself and had two actions! She has another card that says flat out.. \"incap an enemy within 4 range\" lol. Yes its a one shot, but she just does that first and boom, no way to win basically lol.&nbsp;</span><br><br><span>So any help is appreciated, has anyone else tried this?</span><br><br><span>(also I found the rulebook to be fairly horrible. It never has a thorough setup section if you're not playing a scenario. it doesn't seem to cover rules in the right order, just not good. Though the mechanics of the game seem excellent)</span></p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:22.116Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
