        "raw": "<p><span style=\"font-family: verdana, 'lucida grande', arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; line-height: 14.77199935913086px; background-color: rgb(245, 245, 255);\">So my son and I broke it out for the first time tonight (purchased at gencon)&nbsp;</span><br style=\"font-family: verdana, 'lucida grande', arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; line-height: 14.77199935913086px; background-color: rgb(245, 245, 255);\" /><br style=\"font-family: verdana, 'lucida grande', arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; line-height: 14.77199935913086px; background-color: rgb(245, 245, 255);\" /><span style=\"font-family: verdana, 'lucida grande', arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; line-height: 14.77199935913086px; background-color: rgb(245, 245, 255);\">He took citizen dawn without the scenario powers, I took ra. First to 3 incaps wins. (skirmish)</span><br style=\"font-family: verdana, 'lucida grande', arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; line-height: 14.77199935913086px; background-color: rgb(245, 245, 255);\" /><br style=\"font-family: verdana, 'lucida grande', arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; line-height: 14.77199935913086px; background-color: rgb(245, 245, 255);\" /><span style=\"font-family: verdana, 'lucida grande', arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; line-height: 14.77199935913086px; background-color: rgb(245, 245, 255);\">All I can say is it wasn&#39;t even close to a contest. Citizen Dawn won so easily that it was more than ridiculous. So, either the villains aren&#39;t meant to be played in skirmish mode, or we seriously are messing something up.&nbsp;</span><br style=\"font-family: verdana, 'lucida grande', arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; line-height: 14.77199935913086px; background-color: rgb(245, 245, 255);\" /><br style=\"font-family: verdana, 'lucida grande', arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; line-height: 14.77199935913086px; background-color: rgb(245, 245, 255);\" /><span style=\"font-family: verdana, 'lucida grande', arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; line-height: 14.77199935913086px; background-color: rgb(245, 245, 255);\">I mean Citizen dawn puts out a citizen with one action that has 8 health itself and had two actions! She has another card that says flat out.. &quot;incap an enemy within 4 range&quot; lol. Yes its a one shot, but she just does that first and boom, no way to win basically lol.&nbsp;</span><br style=\"font-family: verdana, 'lucida grande', arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; line-height: 14.77199935913086px; background-color: rgb(245, 245, 255);\" /><br style=\"font-family: verdana, 'lucida grande', arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; line-height: 14.77199935913086px; background-color: rgb(245, 245, 255);\" /><span style=\"font-family: verdana, 'lucida grande', arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; line-height: 14.77199935913086px; background-color: rgb(245, 245, 255);\">So any help is appreciated, has anyone else tried this?</span><br style=\"font-family: verdana, 'lucida grande', arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; line-height: 14.77199935913086px; background-color: rgb(245, 245, 255);\" /><br style=\"font-family: verdana, 'lucida grande', arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; line-height: 14.77199935913086px; background-color: rgb(245, 245, 255);\" /><span style=\"font-family: verdana, 'lucida grande', arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; line-height: 14.77199935913086px; background-color: rgb(245, 245, 255);\">(also I found the rulebook to be fairly horrible. It never has a thorough setup section if you&#39;re not playing a scenario. it doesn&#39;t seem to cover rules in the right order, just not good. Though the mechanics of the game seem excellent)</span></p>",
